  "body": "Root cause work for developing-today/code#7098 (the recurring blanking of ~/.claude/.credentials.json).\n\nFINDINGS\n- The only first-party writer of the credentials file in the deployed stack is this module's writeCredential; the quota providers (fork + OpenChamber) and the aggregator gatherer are read-only for this file.\n- The write boundary performed NO validation: writeCredential/buildCredentialsFileContents serialize whatever blob they are handed, merging over the prior file. Reproduced on current main: feeding the helper the exact 2026-11-07 incident shape (access \"\", refresh \"\", expiresAt 0, subscriptionType \"max\") persists it verbatim - access length 0, refresh length 0, expiresAt 0, plan retained.\n- The refresh path also persisted a present-but-empty refresh_token and an expires_in of 0 verbatim. The read side was hardened for this class in #1763/#1765; the write side never was. Task 12770 had not landed this guard (the sibling PR #2172 covers temp-file cleanup only).\n\nFIX\n- New ClaudeCodeCredentialWriteError + assertPersistableOAuthBlob, enforced inside buildCredentialsFileContents so every caller of the serializer and of writeCredential is covered: empty/whitespace access token, present-but-empty/whitespace refresh token, or a non-positive/non-finite expiry is refused by name before any write; the existing file stays byte-identical.\n- refreshAndPersist and the sign-in exchange now reject a present-but-empty refresh_token and a present-but-invalid expires_in as malformed success responses (tokens discarded, file unchanged). Absent fields keep the existing merge behavior.\n- Tokens never appear in any error message.\n\nTESTS\n- 10 new tests: the boundary refusing empty/whitespace access, empty/whitespace refresh, and zero expiry (zero writes/renames recorded); the serializer refusing an empty blob; renewal discarding a 200 with an empty refresh_token, an expires_in of 0, a non-JSON body, and an empty access_token, each with the file byte-identical.\n- bun test test/provider/claude-code-auth.test.ts: 52 pass / 0 fail (happy-path rotation and all prior #1818/#1852 behavior intact). Typecheck shows only the pre-existing secret-service.ts @napi-rs/keyring error, identical on main.",
